# This framework is edited on Windows and judged on Linux: the gate copies the tree into a pinned
# container and runs every check there, and a program file it deploys is read on a Linux machine. A
# file that arrives with CRLF is a different file to both of them, and the difference shows up as a
# finding about the code rather than about the line endings.
#
# There is no rule for a shell script here, and that is deliberate rather than an omission: this
# repository holds no shell at all — the gate, the analyzer check and everything under tool/ are
# Dart programs.

# Normalize all text to LF in the repo AND on checkout, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that MUST be LF, whatever the platform they were written on.
*.yaml    text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.json    text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
*.words   text eol=lf

# Binary artifacts — never touch line endings.
*.tgz   binary
*.gz    binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
